sequenceDiagram
  actor U as User
  participant F as :Frontend
  participant G as :Gems
  participant US as :Users
  participant P as :Google Places API
  participant DB as :Database
  participant LF as :Live Feed
  participant OF as :Frontend (other users)

  Note over U,F: Starts with the place places/{id} picked in the first diagram
  U->>F: confirm adding places/{id}
  F->>+G: POST /gem { name: places/{id}, user's location } + login token
  G->>+US: check the login token
  US-->>-G: the user, or invalid
  opt token valid
    G->>+DB: is places/{id} already a gem
    DB-->>-G: yes or no
    opt not a gem yet
      G->>+P: place details of places/{id}
      P-->>-G: place (location, type, rating, review count), not found, or error
      opt place found and within 200 m of the user
        G->>G: compute the Gem Score
        G->>+DB: insert the gem, added by the user
        DB-->>-G: inserted, duplicate, or an error
        opt inserted
          G->>+LF: publish the new gem
          LF-)OF: gem.added (to each app whose area contains it)
          LF-->>-G: done
        end
      end
    end
  end
  G-->>-F: 201 gem, 401 (login invalid or expired), 409 "Gem already exists.", 422 "Too far from place.", 422 "Place does not exist.", 502 "Google Places unavailable.", or 500 "Add Gem failed."
  alt 201 gem
    F-->>U: the new gem, with its Gem Score, on the map
  else 401 login expired
    F-->>U: back to the sign-in screen
  else 409 already a gem (or added by someone else at the same moment)
    F-->>U: "This place is already a gem", map updated
  else 422 too far
    F-->>U: "Move closer to the place to add it"
  else 422 no such place
    F-->>U: "This place can't be added"
  else 502 or 500
    F-->>U: "Couldn't add the gem, try again"
  end
  Note over U,OF: If the server can't be reached, the Frontend shows "No connection, try again"
